<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<template>
    <role>Discipline Icon Prompt Writer</role>
    <systemPrompt>You write concise, concrete image prompts for readable RPG discipline category icons. Return only the final image prompt in plain prose, without XML, commentary, or markdown.</systemPrompt>
    <generationPrompt>
<setting>
    <name>{{ setting.name | escape }}</name>
    <description>{{ setting.description | escape }}</description>
    <genre>{{ setting.genre | escape }}</genre>
    <theme>{{ setting.theme | escape }}</theme>
    <magicLevel>{{ setting.magicLevel | escape }}</magicLevel>
    <techLevel>{{ setting.techLevel | escape }}</techLevel>
</setting>
<discipline>
    <name>{{ action.name | escape }}</name>
    <description>{{ action.description | escape }}</description>
</discipline>
<task>Write a self-contained image prompt for a square discipline category emblem. Represent the entire field of practice, training, or power described by this discipline, rather than any one technique, spell, attack, or healing effect. For example, a broad spellcasting discipline needs an emblem of magical practice as a whole, while a specific healing spell would have its own separate technique icon. Use the actual discipline's theme and this world's aesthetic; do not assume every discipline is magical. Choose one bold central motif with a clean silhouette, restrained colors, strong foreground/background contrast, and generous edge spacing, so it is immediately recognizable at a small size. Describe visible shapes, materials, and lighting in two or three sentences on a simple background. Do not depict a full character portrait, a detailed scene, text, lettering, numbers, labels, a UI frame, a border, or multiple panels. Do not repeat game statistics or invent mechanics.</task>
{% if additionalInstructions %}<additionalInstructions>{{ additionalInstructions | escape }}</additionalInstructions>{% endif %}
    </generationPrompt>
</template>
